# Frontend Conventions

- Use Next.js App Router and TypeScript.
- Prefer Server Components. Add `"use client"` only when browser APIs, React state, effects, or event handlers are required.
- Keep reusable UI components in `frontend/src/app/components/`.
- Keep shared site constants, navigation data, and reusable content definitions in `frontend/src/app/lib/`.
- Keep page-specific content in the relevant route `page.tsx`.
- Reuse existing components and design tokens before adding parallel components or one-off styles.
- Use semantic HTML elements and native `button` or `a` elements for interactive controls.
- Use `next/link` for internal navigation.
- Use `next/image` for content images when an image is added, with meaningful `alt` text and an appropriate `sizes` value.
- Do not introduce server-only features that conflict with static export without confirming the deployment impact first.
- Do not refactor unrelated files, reorder imports, or reformat surrounding code solely for style consistency.
